      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "New Providence Presbyterian Church, founded in 1780, is the town’s oldest religious building.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.therogersvillereview.com/arts_and_entertainment/article_ad1fca8c-da75-11ee-82fb-0bdc214823b9.html",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The historic Fudge Farm, dating to about 1815, sits just east of Surgoinsville and showcases early Tennessee architecture.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Surgoinsville%2C_Tennessee",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Lyons Store, once a trading post, post office, and Confederate recruiting station, now serves as a reminder of Civil War history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.therogersvillereview.com/arts_and_entertainment/article_ad1fca8c-da75-11ee-82fb-0bdc214823b9.html",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Surgoinsville lies just northeast of Hawkins County’s geographic center, on the north side of the Holston River.",
